ean singer-songwriter and radio presenter. He began his singing career after winning the television talent show Superstar K 4 in 2012. Kim officially debuted with the studio album, Love Love Love (2013), which included the hit single \"Bom Bom Bom.\" The album garnered Kim awards for best new artist at the 15th Mnet Asian Music Awards and the 2014 Golden Disc Awards. Kim followed up his first album with the studio albums, Home (2014) and The Great Dipper (2015), and the extended play, Blooming Season (2017).","title":"Roy Kim","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roy_Kim"}},"Q123156641":{"id":"Q123156641","name":"YeonJi","ko":"연지","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kwak YeonJi","Yeonji","Kwak Yeonji","Kwak Yeon-ji","Gwak Yeonji","Kwak Yeon-Ji"],"birth":"2008-01-08","death":"","birthplace":"Songpa District","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["pop singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q115099831","name":"TripleS","start":"2024","end":""}],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/e9b984ee-2c50-4411-bbaf-bf6ecb4db080"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q12588833":{"id":"Q12588833","name":"Kim Ji-hun","ko":"김지훈","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Ji-hoon"],"birth":"1973-03-21","death":"2013-12-12","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","television actor"],"debut":"1990","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q12621310","name":"Two Two","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Ji-hoon (May 5, 1973 – December 12, 2013) was a South Korean singer, songwriter, record producer, actor, television presenter, and VJ. He is best known as the lead singer of Two Two, a popular Korean pop group from the mid-1990's. He is also known for being the lead singer of Duke, a Korean pop duo formed with Kim Suk-min, a former member of the New Two Two. In the early 2000's, he grew popular for his appearances on talk shows and variety shows. Later in life, however, his career was marked by controversy, as he had been arrested for drug use in both 2005 and 2009. This led to him being sentenced to 10 months in prison and being placed on a list of banned actors by MBC TV.","title":"Kim Ji-hoon (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Ji-hoon_%28singer%29"}},"Q12594913":{"id":"Q12594913","name":"Mad Clown","ko":"매드클라운","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Cho Dong-lim","Mommy Son"],"birth":"1985-03-25","death":"","birthplace":"United States","nationality":["United States"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","record producer","songwriter"],"debut":"2008","agencies":[{"name":"Soul Company","korean":true,"id":"Q7564197","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/anythinggoes85/","x":"https://x.com/real_mad_clown","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/379d302d-8df0-440e-86c0-30cb37d66a3e"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ee/150425_%EB%A7%A4%EB%93%9C%ED%81%B4%EB%9D%BC%EC%9A%B4_02.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:150425_%EB%A7%A4%EB%93%9C%ED%81%B4%EB%9D%BC%EC%9A%B4_02.jpg","author":"mang2goon","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Jo Dong-rim, better known by the stage name Mad Clown, is an American rapper, songwriter, and record producer. He debuted with the single \"Luv Sickness\" in 2008 and released his first extended play, Anything Goes, in 2011. He broke into the mainstream following the release of \"Stupid in Love,\" his hit 2013 collaboration with Soyou of the girl group Sistar. He has since released the extended plays Ferocity (2014), Piece of Mine (2015), Love is a Dog From Hell (2017), and 0 (2020).","title":"Mad Clown","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mad_Clown"}},"Q12613153":{"id":"Q12613153","name":"Lee Hyun-ji","ko":"이현지","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Hyeon-ji"],"birth":"1987-01-1