"Kim Dong-han, also known mononymously as Donghan, is a South Korean singer, songwriter and actor. He first became known for competing in the reality survival show Produce 101 Season 2, and later debuted in the boy band JBJ. Kim made his solo debut with the release of his EP D-Day in June 2018. He is currently a member of South Korean boy band WEi.","title":"Kim Dong-han","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Dong-han"}},"Q483041":{"id":"Q483041","name":"Changmin","ko":"최강창민","birthName":"심창민","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Max","Choikang Changmin","Changmin"],"birth":"1988-02-18","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","model","songwriter"],"debut":"2003","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q192983","name":"TVXQ","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/changmin88/","x":"https://x.com/now_freehug","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/a46732f1-d435-4dec-9d6d-8aa3c7d5a38b"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Shim Chang-min, better known by his stage name Max Changmin (최강창민; Choegang Changmin), is a South Korean singer-songwriter, actor, and a member of the pop duo TVXQ. Born and raised in Seoul, South Korea, Changmin was scouted by an SM Entertainment talent agent when he was fourteen years old. He made his debut as TVXQ's youngest member in December 2003. Fluent in both Korean and Japanese, Changmin has achieved commercial success throughout Asia as the main vocalist of TVXQ. He has also starred in several dramas.","title":"Max Changmin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Max_Changmin"}},"Q489505":{"id":"Q489505","name":"Wheesung","ko":"휘성","birthName":"Choi Hwee-sung","birthNameEn":"Choi Hwee-sung","aliases":["Realslow","Whee Sung","Choi Hwee-sung"],"birth":"1982-02-05","death":"2025-03-10","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","jazz musician","