"id":"Q484449","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q23936742","name":"Pentagon","start":"","end":""},{"id":"Q48937538","name":"M.O.L.A","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"website":"https://soundcloud.com/knnovation/tracks","instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/831x10/","x":"https://x.com/nakedxproud","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@kinoink","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/9a051388-eca6-457c-91b6-0198325d3ef0"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kang Hyung-gu (Korean: 강형구; born (1998-01-27)January 27, 1998), better known as Kino (키노), is a South Korean singer, songwriter, rapper, composer and dancer. He is best known as a member of the boy group Pentagon, which debuted in 2016 under Cube Entertainment. He releases solo music on SoundCloud under the name Knnovation. He is also a member of the musical collective M.O.L.A. Kino released his first single album Pose in 2022, before departing Cube Entertainment the following year. In late 2023, he established a one-man agency Naked, where he began continued releasing music leading up to his first EP If This Is Love, I Want a Refund in 2024.","title":"Kino (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kino_%28singer%29"}},"Q625121":{"id":"Q625121","name":"Lee Jin","ko":"이진","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1980-03-21","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","film actor"],"debut":"1998","agencies":[{"name":"DSP Media","korean":true,"id":"Q489428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q484082","name":"Fin.K.L","start":"1998","end":"2005"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/leejin_321/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/ad6ae9aa-1fa1-4fb9-bcf9-e17876828a1a"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Jin is a South Korean singer and actress. She made her entertainment debut as a member of the K-pop girl group Fin.K.L, along with Lee Hyori, Ock Joo-hyun, and Sung Yu-ri. After Fin.K.L came to an unofficial end in 2002, Lee became an actress.","title":"Lee Jin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Jin"}},"Q62984417":{"id":"Q62984417","name":"Sunha","ko":"선하","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Koo Sun-ha"],"birth":"1999-10-15","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q60992060","name":"Saturday","start":"2018","end":"2019"}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q6791329":{"id":"Q6791329","name":"Matthew Tishler","ko":"","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"","death":"","birthplace":"Toronto","nationality":["Canada"],"height":null,"occupations":["songwriter","record producer","musician","music publisher"],"debut":"2010","agencies":[],"groups":[],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Matthew Tishler is a Canadian songwriter and music producer who has written and produced songs for film, television, radio, stage, and theme parks. He is known for his work with teen pop artists such as Olivia Rodrigo, Sabrina Carpenter, Dove Cameron, Ashley Tisdale, and JoJo Siwa, as well as popular K-pop/J-pop artists like BTS, TWICE, EXO, TVXQ, NCT Dream, ENHYPEN, Taeyeon, Red Velvet, BoA, Namie Amuro, Kumi Koda, EXILE Atsushi, P1Harmony, ZEROBASEONE and Stray Kids . His projects have combined sales of over 25 million units.","title":"Matthew Tishler","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Tishler"}},"Q6824033":{"id":"Q6824033","name":"Kang Chan-hee","ko":"강찬희","birthName":"강찬희","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Chani"],"birth":"2000-01-17","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["film actor","actor","singer","television actor"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"FNC Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q12581039","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q26856852","name":"SF9","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/c_chani_i/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/6f280e46-3eb6-44e6-9572-286734c528f3"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kang Chan-hee, also known by his stage name Chani, is a South Korean singer and actor. He began his career as a child actor, in the television dramas Listen to My Heart (2011), The Innocent Man (2012), The Queen's Classroom (2013), interactive drama Click Your Heart (2016), crime drama Signal (2016), and high-rated drama Sky Castle (2018). In 2015, he was introduced as one of the first members of NEOZ, which was a first group of FNC Entertainment's pre-debut team Neoz School. He debuted in October 2016 with the boy group SF9 and the single \"Fanfare\".","title":"Kang Chan-hee","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kang_Chan-hee"}},"Q9126881":{"id":"Q9126881","name":"Maeng Yun-young","ko":"맹윤영","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Yunyoung"],"birth":"1993-02-15","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q492271","name":"A-Jax","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q97320161":{"id":"Q97320161","name":"Kim Tae-young","ko":"김태영","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Taeyoung","Kim Tae Young","Kim Tae-young"],"birth":"2003-01-27","death":"","birthplace":"Dongchun-dong","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","dancer"],"debut":"2020","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q90628571","name":"Cravity","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/cravity_official/"},"photo":null,"bio":null}}}